In our C library, the function `extract_token(const char *src, char *dst, size_t dst_cap)` copies a whitespace-delimited token from `src` into `dst`, ensuring null termination. A user reported a crash with a specific input. Looking at the code:

```c
size_t extract_token(const char *src, char *dst, size_t dst_cap) {
    size_t i = 0;
    while (src[i] != '\0' && src[i] != ' ') {
        if (i < dst_cap - 1) {   // line 12
            dst[i] = src[i];
        }
        i++;
    }
    dst[i < dst_cap ? i : dst_cap - 1] = '\0'; // line 17
    return i;
}
```

